Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and required materials.',4,'CHE',1),('CHE156','Chemistry Workshop','Chemistry Workshop (CHE156) is a 4-credit course offered through Chemistry. Students engage with core concepts through readings, discussion, structured assessments, and (where applicable) laboratory or project work aligned to department learning outcomes. Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and required materials.',4,'CHE',1),('CHE201','Organic Chemistry I','Structure and reactivity of organic compounds, stereochemistry, and substitution mechanisms. Laboratory introduces synthesis and spectroscopic characterization.',4,'CHE',1),('CHE205','Organic Chemistry II','Carbonyl chemistry, aromatic reactions, biomolecules, and retrosynthesis strategies. Laboratory includes multi-step syntheses.',4,'CHE',1),('CHE301','Biochemistry I','Protein structure, enzyme kinetics, metabolism pathways, and nucleic acids. Designed for chemistry and biology majors heading toward advanced study.',3,'CHE',1),('COM101','Introduction to Programming','Problem decomposition, control structures, functions, and basic data structures using a modern language. Weekly coding labs and collaborative debugging exercises.',4,'COM',1),('COM103','Computer Science And Mathematics Lab','Computer Science And Mathematics Lab (COM103) is a 5-credit course offered through Computer Science And Mathematics. Students engage with core concepts through readings, discussion, structured assessments, and (where applicable) laboratory or project work aligned to department learning outcomes. Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and required materials.',5,'COM',1),('COM110','Data Structures','Lists, stacks, queues, trees, hashing, heaps, and graphs with complexity analysis. Programming-intensive assignments emphasizing correctness and testing.',4,'COM',1),('COM112','Computer Science And Mathematics Methods','Computer Science And Mathematics Methods (COM112) is a 5-credit course offered through Computer Science And Mathematics. Students engage with core concepts through readings, discussion, structured assessments, and (where applicable) laboratory or project work aligned to department learning outcomes. Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and required materials.',5,'COM',1),('COM121','Computer Science And Mathematics Foundations','Computer Science And Mathematics Foundations (COM121) is a 5-credit course offered through Computer Science And Mathematics. Students engage with core concepts through readings, discussion, structured assessments, and (where applicable) laboratory or project work aligned to department learning outcomes. Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and required materials.',5,'COM',1),('COM130','Computer Science And Mathematics Practice','Computer Science And Mathematics Practice (COM130) is a 5-credit course offered through Computer Science And Mathematics. Students engage with core concepts through readings, discussion, structured assessments, and (where applicable) laboratory or project work aligned to department learning outcomes. Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and required materials.',5,'COM',1),('COM139','Computer Science And Mathematics Analysis','Computer Science And Mathematics Analysis (COM139) is a 5-credit course offered through Computer Science And Mathematics. Students engage with core concepts through readings, discussion, structured assessments, and (where applicable) laboratory or project work aligned to department learning outcomes. Consult the official syllabus each term for prerequisites as enforced at registration, grading weights, and requir